1
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,200
(Episode 7)

2
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,960
(This is a work of fiction.)

3
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,120
- Go on, what are you afraid of?
- Go on, don't be shy.

4
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,800
- I'll back you up.
- Be proactive to win her over.

5
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,560
Hi.

6
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,000
Are you free after school tomorrow?

7
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,400
Would you like
to see a movie with me?

8
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,800
Sorry, I have to study.

9
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,600
It's okay.

10
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,840
It's fine, I'll go with you.

11
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:10,000
Yeah, I'm going
to buy his signed photo now.

12
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,800
Okay.

13
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,680
He's so handsome.

14
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,640
Is this really signed by Edison?

15
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:25,840
Of course.

16
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,200
Don't want it?

17
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,760
Fine, plenty of other people
want it.

18
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,880
I want it.

19
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:41,080
- He's really handsome.
- Yeah, he's so cool.

20
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,360
Excuse me, move aside.

21
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,200
What's the matter?

22
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,440
Think you're so tall?

23
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:34,400
Hey!

24
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,480
Don't touch my stuff, you jerk!

25
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,760
You're the jerk,
flirting with my boy!

26
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:41,880
I wasn't flirting.

27
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:44,880
Still denying it?
You were just talking to him.

28
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,000
Don't accuse me!

29
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,520
I hate girls who act like goddesses.

30
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,800
Strip her and take photos!

31
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:54,480
Hey!

32
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:14,520
This is between us.
It's none of your business.

33
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,080
Do you even know her?

34
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,600
You win this time.

35
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,080
Let's go.

36
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,600
Give me back my money.

37
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,560
No!

38
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:53,840
Give it back!

39
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:56,880
Give it back!

40
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,800
Those girls have targeted you.

41
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,160
Consider this a protection fee.

42
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,080
I'd rather die than have no money.

43
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
I want money.

44
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,920
If you need help, come find me.

45
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,440
I'll charge you for every favor.

46
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,520
When are you finally taking me away?

47
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,440
Ditch that girl first,
then we'll talk.

48
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:51,040
Your mom hasn't sent money
for two years.

49
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,040
She won't even answer the phone.

50
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,760
There are only 20,000 dollars left
of the money she gave me.

51
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,720
That's enough for a ticket
to the US for you.

52
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:04,040
The rest will be
for your living expenses.

53
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,120
I'm not going.

54
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:10,240
She paid me
to take care of you back then.

55
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,200
Now that she has stopped paying,

56
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,400
of course I'm sending you back.

57
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,040
She doesn't want me,
so why should I go there?

58
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:23,520
That's between you and her.
It has nothing to do with me.

59
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,360
She said she would come
for you in a few years.

60
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,680
It has been so many years now.

61
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,280
I've done more than enough.

62
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,280
You're here early.

63
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,360
Can we go now?

64
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,240
Yes, let me just grab my bag.

65
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,160
Okay.

66
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,640
- Let's go.
- Careful.

67
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,720
All right.

68
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,400
I've dealt with her.

69
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,800
So when can you...

70
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:05,200
Anytime. It's just a matter
of buying a ticket.

71
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:28,200
Hey, handsome. Got a light?

72
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,440
Need a light?

73
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,320
He took the bait. Call the police.

74
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,720
(Senior)

75
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:58,480
Hello? I just saw a girl
being dragged into a hotel by a man.

76
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:02,880
Yes, she was crying and saying no.

77
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,360
The girl looked very young.

78
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,680
She might be a minor.

79
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,240
They're at the Kowloon Waltz Hotel.

80
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:16,040
Send someone quickly.
I'm worried about her.

81
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,760
Was he arrested?

82
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:38,240
He begged your aunt to bail him out.

83
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,280
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

84
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,280
That's 150 dollars.

85
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:15,360
What? You said
100 dollars last time.

86
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:17,800
I fixed the front part for you too.

87
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:24,400
I can't even tell which handwriting
is yours or mine anymore.

88
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,480
I'm not lying to you.

89
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,360
How can you
hike up the price like that?

90
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,680
Call the police then.

91
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:34,360
Pay up, or I'll confess
to the teacher.

92
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,960
We'll both go down together.

93
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:48,040
Careful, or they won't
hire you again.

94
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,200
He's emigrating anyway.

95
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,800
Of course I'll take the chance
to squeeze one last bit out of him.

96
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,160
That little?

97
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:34,000
What are you doing? Give it back!

98
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,720
Give it back!

99
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,120
Where's Sang?

100
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,200
Why?

101
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,360
Why do I always meet jerks?

102
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:02,240
Am I destined to be alone
for the rest of my life?

103
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,440
I'm here.

104
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,840
Just don't kick me out.

105
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,360
I don't have the money to raise you.

106
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,600
I don't need you to raise me.

107
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,640
I'll earn my own money.

108
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,720
Starting from today,

109
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,840
every dollar you spend on me,

110
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,440
record it in this notebook
as an IOU.

111
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:18,160
I'll make a lot of money
in the future.

112
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,560
(Starting October 15, 2010,
I, Yau Yam Yam, owe...)

113
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:22,600
I'll pay you back with interest.

114
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,720
Lee Lai Shan said...

115
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:40,720
it costs four million dollars
to raise a child.

116
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,560
Where are you going to find
four million to pay me back?

117
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:47,680
I'll earn it.

118
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:53,560
What kind of job
could you do to earn that?

119
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:05,600
Please welcome
our outstanding alumnus,

120
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:10,000
former highest score record holder
of our faculty,

121
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:12,840
Barrister Edward Yeung,

122
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:16,120
to say a few words
to this year's graduates.

123
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:28,440
It's my honor
to congratulate all of you...

124
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:29,840
on your graduation.

125
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,720
It's great to be back.

126
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,280
I still remember...

127
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,760
when I was in your shoes.

128
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,120
I must become
Mr. Yeung's apprentice.

129
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:43,600
But he's so charming,
it'll be hard to focus on work.

130
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:48,920
Forget it. He doesn't
take apprentices.

131
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,240
Let me help you.

132
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,240
Amber, congratulations.

133
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:04,320
Thank you.

134
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,640
Why did you turn down
Crawford's offer?

135
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,000
You got an offer without even
joining their internship program.

136
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,640
Many people would be envious.

137
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,880
Because I decided
to become a barrister.

138
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:15,080
But that's an international firm.

139
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:18,160
In the long run, I'll definitely
earn more as a barrister.

140
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,640
Your answers never disappoint me.

141
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,040
And this is...

142
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,360
My sister.

143
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,760
- Hello.
- Hello.

144
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,800
Studying law is very stressful.

145
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,680
Family support is very important.

146
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,000
With grades as good as yours,

147
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,200
your family must be very supportive.

148
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,160
Of course.

149
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:36,440
I wish you all the best.

150
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,520
How much was this plushie?

151
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,680
No need. It's a gift for you.

152
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:02,120
Didn't you tell your aunt?

153
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,320
I did.

154
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:06,680
She's going to Panyu
with her new boyfriend.

155
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,240
My company.

156
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:23,320
(Sum Ming Investigations)

157
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,720
Only investigations?

158
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,480
Regulars are a different story.

159
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,960
Contact Senior's family.

160
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:43,360
Find out which law firm
has her will.

161
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,640
Okay.

162
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,960
Can you send me their phone number?

163
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,040
What number?

164
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,840
Her family's phone number.

165
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,480
I don't have it.

166
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,720
Haven't you known her
for a long time?

167
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:05,000
We rarely talked
about personal matters.

168
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:10,760
Then how am I supposed to find them?

169
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,680
Figure it out yourself.

170
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,320
Aren't you packing up?

171
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:24,680
For what?

172
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,200
We're going to court.

173
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,400
Oh, right.

174
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,400
But I'm not ready.

175
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,480
What do you mean you're not ready?

176
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:46,080
I just found out Senior passed away.

177
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:51,920
You don't have to go to court.
Handle her matters.

178
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,040
Why is it that she died,

179
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:59,680
but you don't seem sad at all?

180
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:27,080
WKCC386/2025, Kam Yin Pan.

181
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:28,680
Next case, 454.

182
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,520
Your Honor,
I represent the defendant.

183
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:38,080
Your Honor,

184
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:40,440
the prosecution requests
an eight-week adjournment...

185
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,960
until December 3, 2025,

186
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,560
to allow for further
police investigation...

187
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,040
and to obtain laboratory reports.

188
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:50,560
The prosecution is also aware
of the defendant's bail application.

189
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:51,760
We oppose it.

190
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,400
Given the defendant has confessed
to the charges under caution...

191
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:57,360
and the gravity of the case,

192
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:01,720
there is a high risk of absconding
if bail is granted.

193
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:04,360
He may also interfere
with witnesses.

194
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:07,280
Therefore, the prosecution
opposes the defendant's bail.

195
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:12,800
Your Honor,

196
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,960
the defense does not object
to the adjournment,

197
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,560
but we are applying for bail.

198
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,360
Firstly,

199
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:21,480
the defendant has
no prior criminal convictions.

200
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,320
He was born, raised,
and works in Hong Kong.

201
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:28,120
He is a mechanic
and a part-time escort.

202
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:29,880
Furthermore,

203
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:33,000
the defendant was assaulted
by police at the station yesterday,

204
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,400
resulting in his hospitalization.

205
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,960
This is his medical report.

206
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:38,280
I am now submitting it to the court.

207
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,120
Your Honor,

208
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,040
the report shows
that the defendant's face...

209
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,640
sustained multiple contusions
and abrasions.

210
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:52,000
The doctor believes
these were caused by external force.

211
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,360
My instructions
from the defendant are that...

212
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:58,120
he was subjected to police violence
while in custody.

213
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:00,840
As a result, he only admitted...

214
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,120
to the charges involuntarily.

215
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,720
The defendant's occupation is
an escort.

216
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:07,520
His scope of service has always
included sexual services.

217
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:09,360
So we cannot rule out...

218
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:11,360
that the reason
he is being accused of rape...

219
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,720
involves a labor dispute.

220
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:17,440
The defendant is willing
to increase the bail amount.

221
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,640
200,000 dollars in cash bail,

222
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:22,920
with his friend Mr. Mak Tin Lun
acting as a surety...

223
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,520
for another 200,000 dollars.

224
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:28,080
The defendant can report
to Mong Kok Police Station...

225
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,560
every night between 6pm and 9pm.

226
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,480
He will surrender
all travel documents...

227
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:34,000
and promises not to leave Hong Kong
during this period.

228
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:36,160
He will also reside
at his registered address.

229
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:39,400
Furthermore,
the defendant will not...

230
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:42,000
directly or indirectly
contact witnesses.

231
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,520
I urge Your Honor to approve...

232
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:45,920
the defendant's bail application.

233
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:59,400
I can't believe that trick
of hitting the wall actually worked.

234
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,000
Dee has eyes everywhere.

235
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:06,240
Find a place to lay low.
Don't wander off.

236
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:10,320
Actually, I don't
provide sexual services.

237
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,880
What?

238
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,120
As a part-time boyfriend,
I don't provide sexual services.

239
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:18,400
What did you say?

240
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,080
You're a VIP.

241
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,440
Now that we've bought some time,

242
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:38,160
I'll try my best to get the police
to drop the charges.

243
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:41,000
You've already helped me a lot.

244
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,440
I want to handle this myself.

245
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:43,960
How are you going to handle it?

246
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:46,160
Don't worry.
You got me out like this.

247
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:47,600
I've learned a lot.

248
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,200
Bye.

249
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:57,160
Hello?

250
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,600
Hello? I've checked around.

251
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,560
- Senior didn't leave a will.
- Okay.

252
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:05,840
Master.

253
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:08,120
I found Senior's family.

254
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,480
It turns out she...

255
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:10,920
She...

256
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:13,320
- She...
- She what?

257
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:16,520
It turns out
she's the daughter of Counselor Ma.

258
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:21,280
She's the daughter of that jerk?

259
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:23,520
(Protect Children,
Protect Traditional Values)

260
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:24,840
First of all, thank you
to the Glory Society...

261
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:25,840
for inviting me today.

262
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:30,480
The goal of today's press conference
is very clear.

263
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:33,960
Protect our children,
protect traditional values,

264
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,720
and oppose homosexuality.

265
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:38,680
Our society has reached...

266
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:41,800
a critical point where we must stop.

267
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:43,920
If we don't stand up today...

268
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:46,920
and let the virus
in the name of freedom spread,

269
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:49,440
it will not only
destroy our social order,

270
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,440
poison our next generation,

271
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:55,000
but also plunge the world
into a state of no return.

272
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:58,440
Regarding the government's
earlier concession...

273
00:23:58,440 --> 00:23:59,560
to same-sex marriage,

274
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:03,240
allowing them housing subsidies
and inheritance rights,

275
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:04,520
I am very disappointed.

276
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:07,920
Right is right, and wrong is wrong.

277
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:11,440
A wrong thing doesn't
become right...

278
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:12,520
just because
more people are doing it.

279
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:15,800
I am a descendant of the dragon.

280
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:18,040
I'm determined
to protect traditional values...

281
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:19,360
and the traditional family.

282
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,920
I want to speak
for the silent majority.

283
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:23,520
So I'm announcing now...

284
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:26,120
that I've decided to file a lawsuit
in the High Court...

285
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:28,960
for a judicial review of gay rights.

286
00:24:31,200 --> 00:24:33,400
- Mr. Ma.
- Mr. Ma.

287
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,360
Mr. Ma, actually, the whole world...

288
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:36,960
is moving towards equal rights
for sexual minorities.

289
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:39,280
Why do you keep
targeting homosexuals?

290
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:41,520
Didn't I just say?

291
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:44,000
A wrong thing doesn't
become right...

292
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:45,280
just because more people do it.

293
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:48,120
If the whole world hits a wall,
will you follow suit?

294
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:50,680
These ideologies...

295
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:53,200
are completely harmful
and of no benefit...

296
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:55,440
to our economy
and social development.

297
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:58,240
For thousands of years,
China has had...

298
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,960
monogamy between a man and a woman
as the family core.

299
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:03,400
These traditional values cannot
be shaken.

300
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:07,240
But Hong Kong promotes itself
as an international city.

301
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:10,320
Shouldn't we align
with international values?

302
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,520
Which news outlet are you from?

303
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:14,320
I'm a student reporter from HKU.

304
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,000
So you're not a real reporter.

305
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:17,320
A fake reporter.

306
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:19,120
- Please leave.
- I'm not a fake reporter.

307
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:20,640
- Sir, please leave.
- I applied for this.

308
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:21,880
Please leave.

309
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,960
Regarding your question,

310
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:30,840
I believe the world
should align with us,

311
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:32,760
rather than us catering to it.

312
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,360
Next.

313
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:38,280
Mr. Ma, why did you take
this action so suddenly?

314
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:39,760
Is it because the election is
coming up?

315
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:42,760
Rumor has it you were asked
to step aside for a newcomer.

316
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:45,280
Are you doing this
to win over voters...

317
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:46,760
and gain support within the party?

318
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:50,080
Everything I do is
to speak up for justice.

319
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:52,800
I speak out against injustice.
It's as simple as that.

320
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:57,480
Okay, I got it.

321
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:03,200
I can't believe you're late
because of a press conference.

322
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:06,800
I promised them I would
be there. I'm just a little late.

323
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,440
There's no need for the long face.

324
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,400
Is everyone here?

325
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:18,880
Who is that?

326
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:20,160
She's with us.

327
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:21,400
With us?

328
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,880
Sze Ming.

329
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:39,840
Sze Ming, wake up!

330
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:02,360
Did your daughter
have any medical history...

331
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:03,400
before she passed?

332
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:06,280
Wait, I want
to clarify something first.

333
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:10,480
Who are you?

334
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:12,840
Why is she allowed to be here?

335
00:27:15,080 --> 00:27:16,280
I am Sze Ming's family.

336
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:21,160
We are her family.

337
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:25,000
I don't believe I've ever seen you.

338
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:26,720
Enough.

339
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:29,480
Stop it, okay?

340
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:35,160
So did your daughter have
any prior medical history?

341
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,680
She was always very healthy.

342
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:43,960
How could this happen?

343
00:27:46,480 --> 00:27:48,800
Sze Ming was hospitalized
for spasms three years ago.

344
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,440
But they couldn't
find the cause at the time.

345
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:52,560
Also, she had a pollen allergy.

346
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:54,480
She recovered after moving
to Australia for school.

347
00:27:54,560 --> 00:27:55,880
It hasn't recurred since then.

348
00:27:58,360 --> 00:28:01,080
I see. I'll arrange for an autopsy
as soon as possible.

349
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:02,400
That won't be necessary.

350
00:28:04,280 --> 00:28:05,280
Don't cut her open.

351
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:07,360
I understand.

352
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:11,400
The report shows
she suffered a violent impact.

353
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:13,320
Death was almost instantaneous.

354
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,600
I would like to have
Sze Ming's personal effects.

355
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:29,640
All right, I'll have my colleague
arrange that for you.

356
00:28:30,840 --> 00:28:31,840
Thank you.

357
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:36,800
Without an autopsy, it should
take about a few days.

358
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:39,680
You can sign the documents
to claim the body then.

359
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:42,080
All right, thank you.

360
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:48,520
If I want to take the body
out of Hong Kong,

361
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:50,200
what do I need to do?

362
00:28:50,840 --> 00:28:52,040
I believe you can apply
for a permit...

363
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:53,040
from the Births and Deaths
Register Office.

364
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:55,000
You can ask the morgue manager
for the details.

365
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:59,440
Can you explain who this woman is?

366
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:04,960
You want to take Sze Ming away?

367
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,840
It was Sze Ming's last wish
to be buried in Australia.

368
00:29:10,760 --> 00:29:11,920
I want to fulfill it for her.

369
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:14,240
Hey.

370
00:29:15,280 --> 00:29:16,480
That's enough.

371
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,280
Who are you exactly?

372
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:20,000
Stop talking nonsense.

373
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:23,240
I'm Sze Ming's wife.

374
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:25,920
We were legally married
in Australia.

375
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:29,280
I hope you can
respect Sze Ming's decision.

376
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:34,600
Listen carefully.

377
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:36,960
My daughter is not married.

378
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:39,160
She will stay in Hong Kong.

379
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:44,000
According to the Coroners Ordinance,

380
00:29:44,520 --> 00:29:46,800
same-sex partners have the right
to claim the body.

381
00:29:48,320 --> 00:29:50,480
I am her legal next of kin.

382
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:52,320
You are nothing.

383
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:57,720
This is Sze Ming's last wish.

384
00:29:58,680 --> 00:30:00,000
I'll fight for it until the end.

385
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:05,360
Then I'll see you in court.

386
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:27,240
When I get down there,

387
00:30:28,520 --> 00:30:29,680
I'll need your help too.

388
00:30:31,800 --> 00:30:33,120
Please take care of me then.

389
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:08,240
Are you doing okay down there?

390
00:31:10,560 --> 00:31:12,040
I didn't expect you
to really see me.

391
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:16,000
Because I'm also a dying person.

392
00:31:18,560 --> 00:31:21,880
When this line
reaches my heart, I'll die.

393
00:31:25,360 --> 00:31:28,040
Don't ask. I'll tell you
when I get down there.

394
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,440
I know.

395
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:31,040
You know?

396
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:36,040
You're famous down there now...

397
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:38,680
for returning to the mortal realm
to fulfill ghosts' wishes.

398
00:31:39,680 --> 00:31:40,680
No way.

399
00:31:43,600 --> 00:31:44,960
Thanks for burning
so much joss paper for me.

400
00:31:45,760 --> 00:31:47,000
Otherwise, I couldn't have come up.

401
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:50,840
It's the least I could do.

402
00:32:05,440 --> 00:32:06,760
Actually, I'm here this time...

403
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:09,960
because I want you
to help me with a lawsuit.

404
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:12,440
A lawsuit?

405
00:32:24,480 --> 00:32:25,720
Actually, I really like Australia.

406
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:30,960
I've always wanted to live there.

407
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:35,040
I only came back to Hong Kong
to make more money.

408
00:32:35,560 --> 00:32:37,000
I wanted to buy land there,

409
00:32:38,080 --> 00:32:39,680
raise animals, and grow plants.

410
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:47,120
I told my wife...

411
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:51,200
that if I die,

412
00:32:51,960 --> 00:32:54,400
she must bury me
in the Darwin grasslands.

413
00:32:57,240 --> 00:32:59,520
I want to sleep
on the comfortable grass...

414
00:33:00,360 --> 00:33:01,760
and look at the beautiful sky
every day.

415
00:33:10,560 --> 00:33:13,600
So my last wish is
to be buried in Australia.

416
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:19,400
But my dad will definitely refuse.

417
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:21,400
You have to help me deal with him.

418
00:33:22,520 --> 00:33:24,560
I'll tell my wife
to use all our savings...

419
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:25,880
to pay your legal fees.

420
00:33:27,240 --> 00:33:29,600
Anyway, I must go back to Australia.

421
00:33:32,040 --> 00:33:33,040
Don't worry.

422
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:35,440
It's legally permissible.

423
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:42,400
63666989. That's my wife's number.

424
00:33:42,840 --> 00:33:43,960
You must help her.

425
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:53,880
Did you visit your wife in a dream
to tell her I'm coming?

426
00:33:58,040 --> 00:33:59,040
No.

427
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:06,920
I'm not ready to see her yet.

428
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:20,200
I'm sorry.

429
00:34:21,120 --> 00:34:22,120
Sorry for what?

430
00:34:27,160 --> 00:34:28,240
Over the years,

431
00:34:32,560 --> 00:34:34,400
you've done
so many bad things for me.

432
00:34:36,720 --> 00:34:37,800
It shortened your life.

433
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:43,800
I've dragged you down. I'm sorry.

434
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:55,080
The King of Hell said
this was my allotted lifespan.

435
00:34:55,520 --> 00:34:56,520
It has nothing to do with you.

436
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:10,760
I'm leaving.

437
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:14,360
Remember to help me.

438
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:18,200
And burn a few more
packs of cigarettes.

439
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:02,640
You stink.

440
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,160
How many days has it been
since you showered?

441
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:06,920
I'll shower tomorrow morning.

442
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:11,640
Clothes, toothbrush, and towel.
They're all here.

443
00:36:13,240 --> 00:36:14,240
Thank you.

444
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:17,160
Any news?

445
00:36:18,280 --> 00:36:20,200
Please, the first thing
you think about is that woman.

446
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:22,520
Your buddy here is suffering.

447
00:36:22,600 --> 00:36:25,440
The shop is being watched daily.
Business is dead.

448
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:28,640
Her life is on the line.
How can you compare?

449
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Did you find her?

450
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:35,000
Who knew my dad's triad past
would actually be useful?

451
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,080
Dee has many enemies.
He wasn't hard to track.

452
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:42,280
What are you doing?

453
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:45,280
Saving her.

454
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:46,920
Are you crazy?

455
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:48,640
You can't be seen there.

456
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:50,520
I thought you just wanted
to find someone to save her.

457
00:36:52,640 --> 00:36:53,640
Who else would do it?

458
00:36:56,040 --> 00:36:57,840
You should leave. It'll be fine.

459
00:37:06,120 --> 00:37:07,520
Actually, you don't have
to stay with me.

460
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:11,160
Well, now that I know about it,

461
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:12,840
I can't just watch you go
to your death.

462
00:37:17,080 --> 00:37:19,400
She's just a woman.
Don't risk your life.

463
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,600
A guy without a woman like you
wouldn't understand.

464
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,840
Then I really don't understand.

465
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:49,000
When is the delivery arriving?

466
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:51,800
It's here.

467
00:37:57,360 --> 00:37:58,440
Delivery's here.

468
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:01,600
Go!

469
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:30,240
Go upstairs.

470
00:38:35,120 --> 00:38:36,120
Paula.

471
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:41,680
Are you okay?

472
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:37,360
I'm sorry.

473
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:41,440
Sorry to trouble you.

474
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:44,600
Sit down first.

475
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:45,920
Why did you bring a woman
to my house?

476
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:49,320
Hey.

477
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:52,480
I'm afraid Dee will look for me
through everyone I know.

478
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:54,800
I couldn't think of anywhere else.

479
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:57,760
She's Dee's woman?

480
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:01,440
Are you crazy?

481
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:05,560
Take her back right now.

482
00:40:05,640 --> 00:40:07,920
I can't. Her husband will kill her.

483
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,760
If she stays here, you're dead.

484
00:40:11,160 --> 00:40:12,600
Just for one day. Just one day.

485
00:40:13,520 --> 00:40:15,320
Now you're dragging me into this?

486
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:19,080
I'm sorry, but she's
in a terrible state.

487
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:21,240
Just do it out of the kindness
of your heart.

488
00:40:22,400 --> 00:40:23,600
Think of it as earning
some good karma.

489
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:30,200
You've violated your bail conditions
by contacting a witness.

490
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:33,160
I know.

491
00:40:33,200 --> 00:40:35,920
But I can't worry
about that right now.

492
00:40:37,240 --> 00:40:38,680
I'll find her another place later.

493
00:40:38,840 --> 00:40:39,920
Just let her stay for one night.

494
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:42,560
Please.

495
00:40:45,240 --> 00:40:46,240
I'm begging you.

496
00:40:49,640 --> 00:40:50,640
One night.

497
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:54,160
Thank you.

498
00:40:58,600 --> 00:41:00,960
You'll sleep here tonight.
You're safe for now.

499
00:41:02,280 --> 00:41:03,520
I'm leaving now. Bye.

500
00:41:11,480 --> 00:41:13,080
I used to be Dee's lawyer.

501
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:14,320
He really is a madman.

502
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:16,960
I know.

503
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:18,800
Sorry for the intrusion.
